        "paragraphs": [
            "Google Lyria is Google's family of music generation models, available through the Gemini API. Google says Lyria 3.5 is Google's family of music generation models and that with Lyria 3.5 you can generate high-quality, 44.1 kHz stereo audio from text prompts or from images. Google says these models deliver structural coherence, including vocals, timed lyrics, and full instrumental arrangements.",
            "The Lyria family includes Lyria 3 Clip, with model ID lyria-3-clip-preview, which Google says is best for short clips, loops and previews and always generates a 30-second clip in MP3, and Lyria 3.5, with model ID lyria-3.5, which Google says is best for full-length songs with verses, choruses and bridges and lasts a couple of minutes, controllable using prompt. Both models can be used using the new interactions API, supporting multimodal inputs of text and images, and produce 44.1 kHz high-fidelity stereo audio. Google also lists Lyria RealTime, designed for real-time, interactive music generation, and Magenta RealTime, described as Google's Lyria open model.",
            "Google says Lyria is its most advanced AI music generation tool, developed with input from producers and musicians, and that Lyria 3.5 is its latest model with improved vocals, musicality, and variable song lengths. Google offers Lyria through the Gemini API, and says you can try it in Google Flow Music and in Gemini."
        ],
